    {
      "title": "Synthetic Events and the Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Synthetic Events and the Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Event Wrapper",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==SyntheticEvent== = React's cross-browser wrapper around the native event",
                "Raw browser event: `e.nativeEvent`",
                "Same interface in every browser"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handlers and React 17+",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Handlers are ==camelCase== props: `onClick`, `onChange`",
                "Pass a **function reference**; React calls it on the event"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<button onClick={handleClick}>Save</button>",
                "<button onClick={handleClick()}>Save</button>"
              ],
              "note": "second line calls it during render"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Listeners sit on the {blue:root container}, not `document`",
                "{green:No event pooling}: `e` persists, but `e.currentTarget` is null after `await`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which Element, Which Event",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Which element?",
                "`e.target`",
                "`e.currentTarget`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "element that fired",
                  "element with the handler"
                ],
                [
                  "Click on `<b>` in a button",
                  "`<b>`",
                  "`<button>`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Input event",
                "React `onChange`",
                "Native `change`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fires",
                  "every ==keystroke==",
                  "on ==blur=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "`onClick={handleClick()}` runs at render and passes its result. Write `onClick={handleClick}`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled vs Uncontrolled Inputs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Controlled vs Uncontrolled Inputs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Controlled",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Value comes from ==state==; `onChange` updates it",
                "React is the **single source of truth**",
                "Checkbox: `checked` and `e.target.checked`",
                "Select: `value` goes on `<select>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<input value={name} onChange={e => setName(e.target.value)} />"
              ],
              "note": "controlled text input"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Uncontrolled",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The ==DOM== holds the value",
                "Read it on submit: `ref.current.value` or `FormData`",
                "Seed with `defaultValue` / `defaultChecked`",
                "File input is ==always uncontrolled=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const ref = useRef(null);",
                "<input defaultValue=\"Ann\" ref={ref} />",
                "const onSubmit = () => save(ref.current.value);"
              ],
              "note": "uncontrolled: read the ref on submit"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which to Use",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Controlled",
                "Uncontrolled"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Validation",
                  "{green:Instant}",
                  "On submit"
                ],
                [
                  "Disable / format",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "No"
                ],
                [
                  "Re-renders",
                  "Every keystroke",
                  "None"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "Live feedback",
                  "Submit-only forms"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Symptom",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`value` with no `onChange`: read-only field and a warning",
                  "Add `onChange`, or use `defaultValue`"
                ],
                [
                  "`value` goes `undefined` to a string: uncontrolled flips to controlled",
                  "Initialise state with `''`"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Form Submission and preventDefault",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Form Submission and preventDefault",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Triggers Submit",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Put ==onSubmit== on `<form>`, **not** on the button",
                "Enter in a field and a click on a submit button both fire it",
                "`e.preventDefault()` stops the browser's ==full-page reload==, so React handles the submit"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Enter / click",
                    "sub": "submit button",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "onSubmit(e)",
                    "sub": "on the form",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "preventDefault()",
                    "sub": "no reload",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Your code",
                    "sub": "read and save",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading Fields Without State",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`new FormData(e.currentTarget)` collects every field",
                "`Object.fromEntries(data)` gives all values as an object",
                "`data.get('email')` gives a single value",
                "A field needs a ==name== attribute to appear in FormData"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "function onSubmit(e) {",
                "  e.preventDefault();",
                "  const fd = new FormData(e.currentTarget);",
                "  save(Object.fromEntries(fd));",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Button Types and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Button",
                "Submits?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`<button>` (no type)",
                  "{green:Yes}, defaults to submit"
                ],
                [
                  "`type=\"submit\"`",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`type=\"button\"`",
                  "{red:No}, use for non-submitting actions"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Silent bugs",
              "text": "No `name` means the field is **missing** from FormData. A bare `<button>` inside a form **submits** it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Form Actions in React 19",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Form Actions in React 19",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Action Instead of a URL",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<form action={fn}>`: a ==function==, not a URL",
                "React calls `fn(formData)`; default is ==auto-prevented==",
                "Runs in a ==transition==: can be `async`",
                "Uncontrolled fields ==reset== after success",
                "`'use server'` action works ==before hydration==",
                "Controlled inputs: not reset"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Status and Per-Button Actions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useFormStatus()` returns `{ pending, data, method, action }`",
                "Call it in a ==child== of the form, not the form's own component",
                "`formAction` on a button ==overrides== the form action"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "function Submit() {",
                "  const { pending } = useFormStatus()",
                "  return <button disabled={pending}>Publish</button>",
                "}",
                "<form action={save}>",
                "  <Submit />",
                "  <button formAction={saveDraft}>Save draft</button>",
                "</form>"
              ],
              "note": "Submit is rendered inside the form"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. action vs onSubmit",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "action",
                "onSubmit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Data",
                  "`FormData`",
                  "event `e`"
                ],
                [
                  "Reset",
                  "automatic",
                  "manual"
                ],
                [
                  "Pending",
                  "`useFormStatus`",
                  "own state"
                ],
                [
                  "`preventDefault`",
                  "not needed",
                  "required"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "uncontrolled forms",
                  "controlled, custom flow"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Same component",
              "text": "`useFormStatus` in the component that renders `<form>` never sees that form. Move it into a child."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useActionState and Validation Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useActionState and Validation Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Hook",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const [state, formAction, isPending] = useActionState(fn, initialState)`",
                "`fn` is ==(prevState, formData) => newState==",
                "Pass `formAction` to `<form action>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Errors as State",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "async function signup(prev, formData) {",
                "  const values = Object.fromEntries(formData);",
                "  const r = schema.safeParse(values);",
                "  if (!r.success) {",
                "    return { errors: { email: 'Required' }, values };",
                "  }",
                "  return { errors: {}, values };",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "Zod safeParse inside the action"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Return errors as {green:state}, never throw",
                "Render `state.errors.email` next to its field",
                "`defaultValue={state.values?.email}`: React 19 ==resets== uncontrolled fields",
                "Server or action is the {green:source of truth}; client checks are only UX"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Timing and Access",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Submit",
                    "sub": "first",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Blur",
                    "sub": "touched fields",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Change",
                    "sub": "after first error",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`isPending` disables the submit button",
                "`aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby` on fields announce errors"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Errors are ==returned==, values are ==echoed back==, and the server decides."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "React Forms Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "React Forms Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Events and Inputs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`onChange` fires per ==keystroke==",
                "`e.target` fired it; `e.currentTarget` owns the handler",
                "`e.nativeEvent` is the raw DOM event",
                "Pass `onClick={fn}`, not `fn()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Controlled",
                "Uncontrolled"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Wiring",
                  "`value` + `onChange`",
                  "`defaultValue` + ref/FormData"
                ],
                [
                  "Init",
                  "state `''`, not `undefined`",
                  "DOM holds it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Submit: Classic vs React 19",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function onSubmit(e) {",
                "  e.preventDefault();",
                "  const fd = new FormData(e.currentTarget);",
                "  save(Object.fromEntries(fd));",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "inputs need a name to appear in FormData"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "onSubmit",
                "action={fn}"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Gets",
                  "event",
                  "`FormData`"
                ],
                [
                  "preventDefault",
                  "manual",
                  "automatic"
                ],
                [
                  "After",
                  "manual reset",
                  "auto reset, transition"
                ],
                [
                  "Pending",
                  "own state",
                  "`useFormStatus` in a child"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. useActionState and Validation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const [state, formAction, isPending] =",
                "  useActionState(fn, init);",
                "// fn = (prev, formData) => newState",
                "<form action={formAction}>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Server== is the truth; client checks are UX",
                "Return errors as ==state==, not exceptions",
                "Echo values: `defaultValue={state.values?.email}`",
                "`disabled={isPending}` on submit"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Gotcha",
